\[
\frac{0.15\ \text{mL acetic acid}}{100\ \text{mL solution}}
\quad \text{and} \quad
\frac{100\ \text{mL solution}}{0.15\ \text{mL acetic acid}}
\]

For 250 mL of solution:

\[
250\ \text{mL solution}\times \frac{0.15\ \text{mL acetic acid}}{100\ \text{mL solution}}
=0.375\ \text{mL acetic acid}
\]

For 0.035 mL of acetic acid:

\[
0.035\ \text{mL acetic acid}\times \frac{100\ \text{mL solution}}{0.15\ \text{mL acetic acid}}
=23.3\ \text{mL solution}
\]

