The boiling point elevation constant is calculated from

\[
K_b=\frac{R T_b^2 M}{\Delta_{\text{vap}}H}
\]

where \(M\) for cyclohexane is \(84.16\ \text{g mol}^{-1}=0.08416\ \text{kg mol}^{-1}\), and \(\Delta_{\text{vap}}H=29.97\times 10^3\ \text{J mol}^{-1}\).

\[
K_b=\frac{(8.314\ \text{J K}^{-1}\text{mol}^{-1})(354\ \text{K})^2(0.08416\ \text{kg mol}^{-1})}{2.997\times 10^4\ \text{J mol}^{-1}}
\approx 2.93\ \text{K kg mol}^{-1}
\]

FINAL ANSWER: \(K_b \approx 2.93\ \text{K kg mol}^{-1}\)
